    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Adding a skill",
      "prov:value": "**`skill:register`, singular.** Two commands one letter apart existed between\n2026-09-24 and 2026-09-26 — `skill:register` and `skills:register`, built by two\nsessions that each looked for a command and did not find the other's.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-24",
        "2026-09-26"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24",
        "2026-09-26"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "What a skill file owes, and why you cannot see it",
      "prov:value": "The CI job `qa-publish` stores every run's `test/results/`\non the orphan `qa-reports` branch under `main/<sha>/` or `pr/<n>/<sha>/` (arc\n`3fva`)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What a skill file owes, and why you cannot see it",
      "prov:value": "CI judges the *merge* of each pull request's head into the base, so an\nundeclared skill on `main` fails the gate set on **every open pull request** — and\nthe author who sees the failure is whoever opens the next one. Between 2026-09-24\nand 2026-09-26 that happened **seven times**, and seven different sessions each\ndiagnosed it from scratch.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-24",
        "2026-09-26"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24",
        "2026-09-26"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The manifest entry is yours, on purpose",
      "prov:value": "`skill:register` will not add it, and that refusal is the one place the\nconsolidation kept the older design over the newer one."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A new folder is a named subgraph of its harness — declare it",
      "prov:value": "Each has exactly one way to be declared, and the place\nthe folder sits decides which (owner, 2026-10-14):",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-14"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A new folder is a named subgraph of its harness — declare it",
      "prov:value": "Add `subgraph: true` when the new folder is a subgraph\n   of the INSTANCE rather than a part of its parent's graph (bean `cmsl`:\n   `voices` is the first kind, `beans.json`'s `defs` the second).\n3.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean cmsl"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A new folder is a named subgraph of its harness — declare it",
      "prov:value": "**One folder per Tool, always** (bean `tdir`, owner 2026-10-15: *\"migrate\nall impacted repos … to sub-folders as is strongly recommended behaviour\"*).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean tdir",
        "2026-10-15"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "A new folder is a named subgraph of its harness — declare it",
      "prov:value": "A remote\n  mount lays down declared directories only, so an undeclared code folder is\n  missing downstream (the tools layer's `tools/` was, until 2026-10-14). A\n  harness's package `exports` are derived from its declared, shipped `code`\n  directories (`check:package-exports`, bean `7pvn`), so an undeclared one\n  cannot be imported by package name either.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 7pvn",
        "2026-10-14"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why one pass is not enough",
      "prov:value": "`bun test` runs the\ndetangle and `kg-audit` writers, so by the time those checks execute the\nartefacts are already repaired — bean `ymsu`'s blind spot. A chain measured\nthrough `gates` comes out two steps short, and both omissions look correct.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ymsu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why one pass is not enough",
      "prov:value": "**Four separate attempts to recall this list produced four wrong answers**, in\nboth directions: steps named that adding a skill does not stale (they had gone\nred in the same sessions for unrelated reasons), and steps omitted that it does."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why one pass is not enough",
      "prov:value": "`glossary:check` is a *different program* over the SKOS\nprojection. A test asserting \"every check ends in `:check`\" once drove out the\ncorrect pairing and installed the wrong one — and passed."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Do not re-add `roles:`",
      "prov:value": "`roles:` is **retired**. It carried 325 annotations across 140 files, was read by\nnothing, and pointed at actor ids — `reader`, `collaborator`, `owner` — that have\nnever existed in any commit."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Do not re-add `roles:`",
      "prov:value": "If a skill *should* declare who performs it, that is bean `y1w9`, and the field\nhas to be declared before it is written.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean y1w9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Removing or renaming a skill: two orphans, and they are yours",
      "prov:value": "Both were found by breaking the tool rather than by designing it — registering a\nprobe skill and then deleting it produced one of each."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A new folder is a named subgraph of its harness — declare it",
      "prov:value": "- **A folder nothing declares is a folder nothing reasons about.** No check\n  catches it for you: `check:undeclared-files` sweeps the repository root\n  only, so a new undeclared folder inside a harness passes it.\n- **Declared directories are what can be mounted and exported.** A remote\n  mount lays down declared directories only, so an undeclared code folder is\n  missing downstream (the tools layer's `tools/` was, until 2026-10-14). A\n  harness's package `exports` are derived from its declared, shipped `code`\n  directories (`check:package-exports`, bean `7pvn`), so an undeclared one\n  cannot be imported by package name either. A from-within id cannot yet be\n  mounted on its own: `remote-mount` reads top-level entries only (bean\n  `2j2r`, needed by `mo75`).\n- `bun run cat harness:dirs` then materialises every declared directory, so\n  the folder exists in every checkout rather than only in yours.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 2j2r"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "What a skill file owes, and why you cannot see it",
      "prov:value": "**The `kg-qa` sidecar is a derived QA result, and its record is no longer the\ncommitted file.** The CI job `qa-publish` stores every run's `test/results/`\non the orphan `qa-reports` branch under `main/<sha>/` or `pr/<n>/<sha>/` (arc\n`3fva`). The file is still committed on `main` until bean `5hox` removes it,\nand `kg:audit:check` still reads it, so `skill:register` still writes it —\nbut a judgement about your skill (an agent's voice review, a pair\nattestation) does not go in it: that is `test/attestations/kg-qa/…`, on `main`,\nbecause no writer can regenerate it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 5hox"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A new folder is a named subgraph of its harness — declare it",
      "prov:value": "- **A folder nothing declares is a folder nothing reasons about.** No check\n  catches it for you: `check:undeclared-files` sweeps the repository root\n  only, so a new undeclared folder inside a harness passes it.\n- **Declared directories are what can be mounted and exported.** A remote\n  mount lays down declared directories only, so an undeclared code folder is\n  missing downstream (the tools layer's `tools/` was, until 2026-10-14). A\n  harness's package `exports` are derived from its declared, shipped `code`\n  directories (`check:package-exports`, bean `7pvn`), so an undeclared one\n  cannot be imported by package name either. A from-within id cannot yet be\n  mounted on its own: `remote-mount` reads top-level entries only (bean\n  `2j2r`, needed by `mo75`).\n- `bun run cat harness:dirs` then materialises every declared directory, so\n  the folder exists in every checkout rather than only in yours.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean mo75"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-14"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
